{"title":"Scicon Sports Unveils New Aeronda Cycling Sunglasses With Patented Multispherical Lens","link":"https://bikerumor.com/scicon-sports-unveils-new-aeronda-cycling-sunglasses-with-patented-multispherical-lens/","date":1795634579000,"content":"<p><img src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Eclipse-1536x1024.jpeg\" width=\"1536\" height=\"1024\" alt=\"(All photos / Scicon Sports)\" /></p>\n<p>Scicon Sports, the official eyewear sponsor of UAE Team Emirates and Tadej Pogačar, just launched its latest cycling sunglasses, the Aeronda. The model name describes the lens and combines the words air and wave — onda means wave in Italian. These new performance shades are built around Scicon’s exclusive, patented MasterBlank lens, which combines a “multispherical” shape with outward-facing “flaps” across the top and bottom.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Additionally, the vented MasterBlank lens has a wraparound shape, temple attachments integrated into the lens, and Tactigrip temples/arms and FlexiFit 2.0 nose pad to optimize the fit. The Aeronda is currently offered in four multimirror lens colors, along with a low-light pink, and Scicon provides two options for prescription lenses.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-Design.jpeg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1333\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-Design.jpeg\" alt=\"a person holding the Scicon Aeronda glasses with some design drawings of the glasses in the background\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-Design.jpeg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-Design-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-Design-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-Design-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-Design-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-Design-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-Design-720x480.jpeg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-Design-1350x900.jpeg 1350w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>Aeronda Development</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Scicon says the Aeronda project started in April of 2026 when Tadej Pogačar raced Paris-Roubaix with a special lens fitted to his <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/tadej-pogacar-debuts-new-scicon-sports-aeroshade-2-0-titanium-cycling-sunglasses-with-strade-bianche-victory/\">Aeroshade 2.0 Titanium glasses</a>. This lens featured an outward-facing flap across the bottom, which was intended to help protect the face from dust, mud, debris, water, and generally harsh conditions experienced by riders racing the Hell of the North. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Hero.jpeg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1333\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Hero.jpeg\" alt=\"studio image of the Scicon Aeronda glasses with a black background\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Hero.jpeg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Hero-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Hero-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Hero-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Hero-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Hero-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Hero-720x480.jpeg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Hero-1350x900.jpeg 1350w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>MasterBlank</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>This experimental lens was the basis for what Scicon refers to as MasterBlank: “<em>an oversize, multi-spherical Base 8 patent-pending lens that integrates to the temple attachments directly</em>.” The brand states this new lens design is not a standard lens, and it is not available to other eyewear makers. Instead, it was designed and is owned by Scicon Sports and is exclusive to the brand.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>If you’re into performance eyewear, then you’re probably familiar with the most common cylindrical and spherical lens shapes — and possibly toric too. So what the heck is a multispherical lens? According to Scicon, “<em>It combines several spherical curves in a single continuous surface, and each zone has the right curve for its job: wrapping the face, protecting the eyes, working with the flow of air</em>.”</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Gallery.jpeg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1333\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Gallery.jpeg\" alt=\"a man wearing the Scicon Aeronda sunglasses\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Gallery.jpeg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Gallery-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Gallery-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Gallery-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Gallery-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Gallery-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Gallery-720x480.jpeg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Gallery-1350x900.jpeg 1350w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The MasterBlank lens geometry, a base-8 monolens with a radius of curvature of 66mm, reportedly delivers uniform vision across the whole lens. Meanwhile, the wraparound curve follows the shape of the head, for a streamlined fit and unobstructed peripheral vision. Additionally, the temple attachments are integrated into the lens, a design intended to enhance structural integrity, stability, and security while riding. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Aero.jpeg\"><img width=\"1532\" height=\"1021\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Aero.jpeg\" alt=\"a man wearing the scicon aeronda sunglasses with the wave profile overlaid on them\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Aero.jpeg 1532w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Aero-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Aero-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Aero-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Aero-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Aero-720x480.jpeg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Aero-1350x900.jpeg 1350w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3>Lens “Flaps”</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Beyond the multispherical shape of the lens, the “flaps” are arguably the most visually apparent feature of the new Aeronda sunglasses. These flaps, as Scicon calls them, are outward-flared portions of the lens, which help to give the glasses their distinctive look and “wave” profile. Scicon claims each flap, upper and lower, also serves a function.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>According to Scicon, “<em>The upper Aero Flap follows the brow line and deflects airflow toward the helmet: it is designed to reduce turbulence in the upper part of the field of view and to keep the eyewear stable at speed.</em> <em>The lower Safety Flap extends the lens downward to protect the face and reduce the risk of cuts in a crash. At the same time, it channels air cleanly around the lower part of the face.</em>”</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Flaps.jpeg\"><img width=\"2415\" height=\"1610\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Flaps.jpeg\" alt=\"a rendering showing the upper and lower flaps of the Aeronda lens\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Flaps.jpeg 2415w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Flaps-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Flaps-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Flaps-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Flaps-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Flaps-2048x1365.jpeg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Flaps-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Flaps-720x480.jpeg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Flaps-1350x900.jpeg 1350w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3>Ventilation</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>The upper and lower edges of the lens also include what Scison calls VortexFlow ventilation. These slim vents are designed to allow air to circulate and reduce fogging, of course, and the brand says they’ve been designed to not let any distracting sunlight in.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Vortexflow.jpeg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1333\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Vortexflow.jpeg\" alt=\"an image and graphic demonstrating the VortexFlow ventilation\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Vortexflow.jpeg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Vortexflow-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Vortexflow-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Vortexflow-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Vortexflow-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Vortexflow-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Vortexflow-720x480.jpeg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Vortexflow-1350x900.jpeg 1350w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3>Adjustability</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>As mentioned above, the temple attachments are integrated into the lens design and make a sturdy fixing point for the temples/arms. Scicon says, “<em>The diamond-pattern TactiGrip temples are made from high-quality flexible nylon, with TPE co-injected tips, and a metal core that adjusts to the millimeter</em>.” Additionally, the FlexiFit 2.0 nose pad features the same TactiGrip thermopolymer with an adjustable design that can be adapted to varying nose bridges and face shapes quickly and easily.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-dimensions.jpeg\"><img width=\"1400\" height=\"1400\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-dimensions.jpeg\" alt=\"dimensions of the scicon aeronda m1\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-dimensions.jpeg 1400w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-dimensions-297x297.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-dimensions-120x120.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-dimensions-768x768.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-dimensions-900x900.jpeg 900w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1.jpeg\"><img width=\"1400\" height=\"1400\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1.jpeg\" alt=\"studio image of the Scicon Aeronda M1\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1.jpeg 1400w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-297x297.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-120x120.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-768x768.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-900x900.jpeg 900w\" /></a></figure>\n<figcaption>The Scicon Aeronda M1.</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3>Sizes</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>The Aeronda sunglasses come in two shapes/sizes, M1 and M3, which look nearly identical, but have very slight differences. The M1 lens is slightly taller at 66mm, has lower vents, and a more shapely upper and lower lens. The M3 lens is a touch shorter at 63mm, does not have lower vents, and has smoother lines to its upper and lower edges.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-dimensions.jpeg\"><img width=\"1400\" height=\"1400\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-dimensions.jpeg\" alt=\"dimensions of the scicon aeronda m3\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-dimensions.jpeg 1400w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-dimensions-297x297.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-dimensions-120x120.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-dimensions-768x768.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-dimensions-900x900.jpeg 900w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3.jpeg\"><img width=\"1000\" height=\"1000\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3.jpeg\" alt=\"studio image of the Scicon Aeronda M3\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3.jpeg 1000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-297x297.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-120x120.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-768x768.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-900x900.jpeg 900w\" /></a></figure>\n<figcaption>The Scicon Aeronda M3.</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3>Lens Options</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>At launch, the Aeronda is available in a total of five different lens options. There are four multimirror colors: Silver, Red, Blue-Green, and Yellow, all of which offer Cat 3 protection and are designed for bright light conditions. Additionally, a Cat 1 Pink version is available as a low-light option. Scicon says that more color variants and a photochromic option are in the works. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-Optical-insert.jpeg\"><img width=\"2212\" height=\"1475\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-Optical-insert.jpeg\" alt=\"studio image of the Scicon Aeronda sunglasses with the SlideFit optical insert\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-Optical-insert.jpeg 2212w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-Optical-insert-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-Optical-insert-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-Optical-insert-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-Optical-insert-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-Optical-insert-2048x1366.jpeg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-Optical-insert-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-Optical-insert-720x480.jpeg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M3-Optical-insert-1350x900.jpeg 1350w\" /></a><figcaption>SlideFit optical insert.</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3>Prescription Lenses</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>For those who require corrective lenses, Scicon has two options for the Aeronda glasses. First, the SlideFit optical insert can be fitted over the nose piece. Second, the Prescription Insert Lens System (P.I.L.S.) integrates a prescription lens directly into the lens of the Aeronda sunglasses for a clean, single-piece solution. P.I.L.S. is an option in the Silver and Red lenses only.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Prescription-scaled.jpeg\"><img width=\"2560\" height=\"1707\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Prescription-scaled.jpeg\" alt=\"studio image of the Scicon Aeronda sunglasses with the P.I.L.S. lenses insert\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Prescription-scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Prescription-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Prescription-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Prescription-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Prescription-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Prescription-2048x1365.jpeg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Prescription-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Prescription-720x480.jpeg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Aeronda-M1-Prescription-1350x900.jpeg 1350w\" /></a><figcaption>P.I.L.S. integrates prescription lenses into the sunglass lens.</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>Pricing and Availability</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Scicon’s new Aeronda cycling sunglasses are priced at €170 / $195. They are available now at select retailers or directly from Scicon Sports.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><em><a href=\"https://sciconsports.com/\">sciconsports.com</a></em></p>","author":"Jeremy Benson","comments":"https://bikerumor.com/scicon-sports-unveils-new-aeronda-cycling-sunglasses-with-patented-multispherical-lens/#respond","siteTitle":"Bikerumor","siteHash":"49f427af0a926f4232eb837006841d7242e153e3afbb590f32e4b104ea3e2718","entryHash":"60deb601d12fa2f8a8956d6951b95f7a00e670de1d2b84ae775c1343d8c82d55","category":"Cycling"}